Notebook[{
Cell["Film Groups", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"ab1b9654-5f7d-44de-9b41-21795920c5f7"],

Cell["The 275 space-time symmetry groups of the plane, animated", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"648e52e3-e1ea-40b4-8aed-963257f3fb54"],

Cell["\<\
A film is a map from spacetime \[DoubleStruckCapitalR]\.b2\[Times]\
\[DoubleStruckCapitalR] to colors. A film group is a crystallographic group \
of symmetries of such a film: transformations g : (x, t) \[RightArrow] (M.x + \
v, s\[ThinSpace]t + \[Tau]), with M a 2\[Times]2 point operation, v a spatial \
translation, s = \[PlusMinus]1 a time direction, and \[Tau] a time offset, \
containing a lattice of two independent spatial translations and one time \
period. Up to crystallographic equivalence there are exactly 275 such groups \
(Ke & Wu, arXiv:2604.05619) \[LongDash] the space-time analogue of the 17 \
wallpaper groups, and a subfamily of the 230 space groups read with one axis \
as time (Fletcher, Math. Gazette 40 (1956) 15\[Dash]19; the 1+1-dimensional \
count of 13 is in Xu & Wu, Phys. Rev. Lett. 120, 096401 (2018)).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"37c7a3c3-40ff-4873-9147-eb186eede09a"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook accompanies the FilmGroups package, a port of the interactive \
atlas at https://yaroslavvb.github.io/animated-groups-fable . Every group is \
stored as exact data, machine-verified against the group axioms, and rendered \
as a looping animation: the orbit of a single animated motif under the group.\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bbdf8b88-27ae-499d-a211-7c61b4438a6b"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"fc3bbded-1504-4085-ae1b-f4f1183277ac"],

Cell["\<\
Place FilmGroups.wl and FilmGroupsData.wl in the same directory as this \
notebook and load:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"903e3e87-5e8c-4d94-834e-8a1621272491"],

Cell["\<\
SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]];
Get[\"FilmGroups.wl\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8e151cd3-757e-43ca-aa4e-2e8ea031f69e"],

Cell["The motif: a clock that cannot alias", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a0834d49-0ab8-4b9c-bad0-3287d104f699"],

Cell["\<\
Each copy of the motif displays its own internal time \[Theta] = \
s\[ThinSpace](t \[Minus] \[Tau]): a vessel that fills once per period, its \
surface marked in red. The fill level is an injective function of \[Theta] \
mod 1, and it cannot be rotated \[LongDash] so two copies at different \
internal times always look different in a frozen frame, no matter how the \
pattern's own rotations act. Orientation and phase are independent readouts. \
The vessel is chiral and asymmetric (no accidental symmetry), and \
time-reversed copies drain instead of filling.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"647f7304-d3e2-4986-82bc-dfb6ea7132bc"],

Cell["Row[Table[FilmGroupMotif[\[Theta]], {\[Theta], 0, 5/6, 1/6}], \
Spacer[4]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"50851768-c031-4f0b-a01e-54cf64af875a"],

Cell["Animating a group", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"14b377a6-a9d3-4469-8fc2-55a006a18ed0"],

Cell["\<\
FilmGroupAnimation accepts an index 1\[Dash]275, an ID like \"g95\", or a \
notation symbol from the catalog. Group #95 is 4\:20824\:20822, the film \
analogue of the space group P4\:2082: a fourfold time screw \[LongDash] each \
quarter turn about a 4\:2082 centre advances the film by half a period. Press \
play.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9f952750-d413-4c00-ae70-912529f6ae13"],

Cell["FilmGroupAnimation[95]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"6efccabb-ca06-4125-a487-834d82b173dc"],

Cell["\<\
A hexagonal time screw, 6\:20823\:20822 (#244): the sixfold centres advance \
the film by a third of a period per sixth of a turn, so equal fill levels \
spiral around each centre.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b43d273d-43a3-476b-a833-26e3aae6fb37"],

Cell["FilmGroupAnimation[\"g244\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a756724f-5660-4606-9f9e-1f6ff357b36c"],

Cell["\<\
Time reversal. In group #2 \[LongDash] o/m\[Prime] over the wallpaper group \
cm \[LongDash] a mirror runs the film backwards: each copy's mirror image \
drains as the copy fills.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36285c4f-f4aa-44c8-a8af-8a78b3222598"],

Cell["FilmGroupAnimation[2]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4c21b6a7-719b-4324-b23d-4cfceca6f80c"],

Cell["\<\
In o/1\[Prime] (#12) the reversal fixes every site, so each vessel is drawn \
superimposed with its own time-reverse and shows two surface lines \
\[LongDash] one rising, one falling \[LongDash] meeting twice per period.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2a23be2e-251a-4bb6-916d-617ef402816f"],

Cell["FilmGroupAnimation[12]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"534ec77e-36b6-4fad-bc69-f775c9c193a5"],

Cell["\<\
The animations are Manipulates with SaveDefinitions \[Rule] True, so they \
keep working \[LongDash] play button and all \[LongDash] in a notebook opened \
without the package.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"43aa95e0-d60e-47ff-af51-2a4ddb3f16b6"],

Cell["Window size and other options", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6a8f6b2d-f057-4737-ac7f-72dc315bd0c4"],

Cell["\<\
\"Cells\" sets the width of the window in lattice translations; the default \
Automatic sizes the window so roughly 16 copies are visible. \"ShowCell\" \
overlays the lattice. A frame at a single time t is a Graphics:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a5540a6c-ead6-497c-8bf8-c21873b22eb6"],

Cell["\<\
GraphicsRow[{FilmGroupFrame[95, 0.3, \"Cells\" -> 2],
  FilmGroupFrame[95, 0.3, \"Cells\" -> 4, \"ShowCell\" -> True]}, ImageSize \
-> 600]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"97e81105-c9a7-409a-b45e-8243be7c8eaa"],

Cell["\<\
\"MotifScale\" shrinks the stamps, \"Colors\" overrides any of \"Body\", \
\"Outline\", \"Fill\", \"Line\", \"Background\", and Background and ImageSize \
pass through to Graphics.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e82cee9c-8684-4ceb-b864-6c06daeef217"],

Cell["\<\
FilmGroupFrame[258, 0.25, \"Cells\" -> {6, 3}, \"MotifScale\" -> 0.9,
  \"Colors\" -> <|\"Fill\" -> RGBColor[\"#8c4a3a\"], \"Line\" -> \
RGBColor[\"#1a3a5c\"]|>,
  ImageSize -> 640]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cb78e716-3335-4d92-8596-880308bcbf04"],

Cell["Browsing all 275", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"079215d6-c002-4223-97c5-11f456a519cb"],

Cell["\<\
The browser steps through the whole catalog (requires the package loaded in \
the current session):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aed9a4ee-2ee6-4c92-b6ef-fa59575e2a87"],

Cell["FilmGroupBrowser[]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d08f5b48-2356-4b8e-9dd1-a2935b6ede52"],

Cell["The catalog", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f76ce3aa-318f-4524-ab29-9a81a166bf1b"],

Cell["\<\
FilmGroupData[] is the full catalog as a Dataset. Each entry records the \
notation Symbol (Conway orbifold notation with time decorations: gyration \
subscripts n\:2096 for time screws, \[Tilde] for time glides, \[Prime] for \
time reversal, c/r prefixes for space-time-centred lattices \[LongDash] see \
the atlas notation page), the crystal System, the base wallpaper group of the \
spatial projection, the flags ForwardTime / Product / Symmorphic, \
human-readable Generators, and the exact rendering spec (Basis, Ops, \
BasePoint).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"51102f38-2645-466b-b083-1e66fd6a4e67"],

Cell["FilmGroupData[]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d198746c-253e-4fad-aa42-a0f3ce00f898"],

Cell["Normal @ FilmGroupData[][GroupBy[\"System\"], Length]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f904e1f3-ef6e-4eaa-830f-8e71b4af2843"],

Cell["\<\
FilmGroupData[][Select[#ForwardTime && ! #Symmorphic &], Length]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"33c35acc-4e1e-4206-8f66-d66e13147dfe"],

Cell["Column @ FilmGroupData[95, \"Generators\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cf0a515c-1b3f-406a-aea5-d5464ed185b9"],

Cell["Verified symmetry", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ff02c498-a8aa-46a7-bce3-94516cfe2a00"],

Cell["\<\
\"Ops\" lists coset representatives of the group modulo \
\[DoubleStruckCapitalZ]\.b2\[Times]\[DoubleStruckCapitalZ] (lattice and time \
period), stored exactly \[LongDash] integer matrices, rational offsets, \
Sqrt[3]/2. VerifyFilmGroup checks identity, inverses and closure in exact \
arithmetic. The whole catalog passes:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"94d2e8a4-b5d6-4e65-8a54-99dd41d8fa40"],

Cell["AllTrue[Range[275], VerifyFilmGroup[#][\"OK\"] &]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"90519074-03f1-4432-a36d-bc2402043da0"],

Cell["\<\
Rendering then inherits the symmetry by construction: a frame is drawn as the \
explicit orbit of the base motif under these representatives and the lattice, \
so applying any listed operation to the picture at time t reproduces the \
picture at time s\[ThinSpace]t + \[Tau] exactly.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2eaae548-6870-482c-926f-cf9d3d4ad1f9"],

Cell["Exporting", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cd2633cd-61e9-424b-be12-3a0fc8140bd0"],

Cell["\<\
Frames export to an animated GIF (here 40 frames, 4 seconds per period, \
matching the atlas):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b8a44970-fb02-4eb3-9d17-a2c95be4ee46"],

Cell["\<\
Export[\"film-group-95.gif\", FilmGroupFrames[95, 40, ImageSize -> 320],
  \"DisplayDurations\" -> 0.1, \"AnimationRepetitions\" -> Infinity]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a6858f2c-3668-415d-9394-c2177621c438"],

Cell["References", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c6346603-8f48-4a93-8380-09f2ff3ce2c2"],

Cell["\<\
T. J. Fletcher, \"Film Groups\", Math. Gazette 40 (1956) 15\[Dash]19. \
doi:10.2307/3610262
S. Xu, C. Wu, \"Space-Time Crystal and Space-Time Group\", Phys. Rev. Lett. \
120, 096401 (2018). arXiv:1703.03388
C. Ke, C. Wu, \"Two-Dimensional Space-Time Groups: Classification and \
Applications\" (2026). arXiv:2604.05619
J. H. Conway, H. Burgiel, C. Goodman-Strauss, The Symmetries of Things (2008) \
\[LongDash] orbifold notation.
Interactive atlas: https://yaroslavvb.github.io/animated-groups-fable
Source: https://github.com/yaroslavvb/animated-groups-fable (wolfram/ \
directory; the catalog data is generated from the atlas's own, and the two \
renderers agree frame by frame).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"95ae0543-84a2-4136-8686-ce74bafd98cc"]
},
WindowSize->{900, 800},
FrontEndVersion->"14.2 for Mac OS X x86 (64-bit) (March 16, 2025)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"9c92d327-3738-4abc-ab9a-eb9d87ea1b9a"
]
